{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02005",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.99,
      "end_seconds": 3.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.71,
      "end_seconds": 10.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Hi doctor, uh, I got here as fast as I could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.85,
      "end_seconds": 17.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.5,
      "end_seconds": 24.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit. What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.09,
      "end_seconds": 34.62,
      "duration_seconds": 8.53,
      "text": "It's pain in my back and hips. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.42,
      "end_seconds": 43.95,
      "duration_seconds": 7.53,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.61,
      "end_seconds": 55.9,
      "duration_seconds": 10.29,
      "text": "Let me think, I take tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night for the prostate. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.41,
      "end_seconds": 57.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.15,
      "end_seconds": 68.64,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "I'm on paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed. Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, maybe, twice a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.72,
      "end_seconds": 74.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.72,
      "end_seconds": 77.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "No, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.14,
      "end_seconds": 96.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.75,
      "end_seconds": 101.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "It's been like this since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.46,
      "end_seconds": 106.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.15,
      "end_seconds": 112.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Hmm, I get some relief from regular tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.6,
      "end_seconds": 116.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.54,
      "end_seconds": 121.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "It, It happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.55,
      "end_seconds": 123.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Does anything set it off?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.45,
      "end_seconds": 131.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I notice it more with moving."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.41,
      "end_seconds": 136.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Alright, rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.34,
      "end_seconds": 150.11,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "Maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day. Well, I was feeling sick at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.97,
      "end_seconds": 155.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Any confusion, bleeding, shortness of breath or vomiting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.07,
      "end_seconds": 163.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "No confusion, bleeding, shortness of breath or vomiting, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.66,
      "end_seconds": 170.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.78,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.34,
      "end_seconds": 173.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.78,
      "end_seconds": 177.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.34,
      "end_seconds": 191.07,
      "duration_seconds": 12.73,
      "text": "I've had an enlarged prostate, yes. Oh, I've got arthritis in my knees. I took the morning off to come in today. Yes, heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.24,
      "end_seconds": 200.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.45,
      "text": "Sure. Yes, an enlarged prostate and arthritis in your knees are known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.16,
      "end_seconds": 218.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.67,
      "end_seconds": 224.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Yes, I had a triple bypass, eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.52,
      "end_seconds": 229.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.15,
      "end_seconds": 236.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "I'm allergic to plasters, I get a red itchy rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.32,
      "end_seconds": 241.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.95,
      "end_seconds": 253.83,
      "duration_seconds": 11.88,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling. My husband and I live above the shop. I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.87,
      "end_seconds": 258.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.74,
      "end_seconds": 269.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.68,
      "end_seconds": 297.98,
      "duration_seconds": 12.3,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 113 over 77, heart rate 81, SpO2 97 percent on room air, height 159 centimetres, temperature 36.9, weight 57 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.8,
      "end_seconds": 301.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.71,
      "end_seconds": 305.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.29,
      "end_seconds": 312.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.67,
      "end_seconds": 316.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.24,
      "end_seconds": 332.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft and you look comfortable and thin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.79,
      "end_seconds": 338.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.68,
      "end_seconds": 371.34,
      "duration_seconds": 15.66,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? It points towards cancer pain needing better control. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Opioid-induced constipation is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.87,
      "end_seconds": 373.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.53,
      "end_seconds": 398.72,
      "duration_seconds": 23.19,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like cancer pain needing better control. Let's use senna, 15 milligrams, at night, long term. It's for opioid-induced constipation. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.02,
      "end_seconds": 400.93,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.87,
      "end_seconds": 405.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Alright, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.73,
      "end_seconds": 412.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 414.19,
      "end_seconds": 415.44,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}